<title>USA: Diamond Shamrock raises U.S. posted crude prices.</title>
<headline>Diamond Shamrock raises U.S. posted crude prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diamond Shamrock Inc said it had raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents, effective Monday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.50 a barrel and Oklahoma sweet to $18.00 a barrel.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
